      domain: 'EHS',
      jurisdiction: 'CENTRAL',
      stateCode: null,
      title: 'Design code and pressure',
      description:
        '1. Ensure that the vessels are designed, constructed and tested in accordance with the Indian standard 2825, ASME Section Mil Division 1 or Division 2. PD5500. EN 13458. EN 13530. AD:2000 code as amended from time to time or such other standard or code approved by the chief controller.\n\n2. Ensure that the design pressure of vessel is not less than: -\n\n(a). The vapour pressure of the gas in the vessel at 55dc if the vessel is meant for the storage of liquefiable gases, (Provided that if the vessel is insulated the vapour pressure of the gas in the vessel shall correspond to the maximum temperature that is likely to be attained by the gas in the vessel);\n(b). The developed pressure of the gas in the vessel at 55dc if the vessel is meant for the storage of a permanent gas.\n\n(c) the maximum allowable service pressure with additional allowances for vacuum and static head or surge due to acceleration or deceleration, as the case may be. in respect of the cryogenic liquid proposed to be stored or transported.\n\nEnsure that:\n(i) The static head (higher of the water column or the compressed gas column) is considered for static pressure vessels.\n(ii) The wind load, seismic loads is considered for vertical cylindrical vessels and horton spheres.',
      applicabilityText:
        'Every person involved in designing, constructing or testing of pressure vessels',
      criticality: 'HIGH',
      timelineType: 'ONGOING',
      recurrenceRule: {
        kind: 'ONGOING_REVIEW',
        every: 'QUARTER',
      },
      ruleStatus: 'CONFIRMED',
      evidenceRequired: false,
