      domain: 'EHS',
      jurisdiction: 'CENTRAL',
      stateCode: null,
      title: 'Filling Capacity and Filling Pressure',
      description:
        '1. Ensure that the maximum quantity of liquefiable gas filled into any vessel is limited to the filling density of the gas and that the vessel is not liquid-full due to expansion of the contents with rise of the temperature to 55dc.\n\n2. Ensure that no vessel is filled with any permanent gas in excess of its design pressure.\n\n3. Ensure that:\n(a) the water capacity of the cryogenic pressure vessel shall be rated in terms of gross water capacity and the allowable water capacity in litres at 15°C.\n(b) the usable water capacity shall not exceed 95% of the gross water capacity.\n(c) an overflow pipe shall be provided at the maximum allowable capacity level as a safeguard against filling the vessel beyond the maximum usable capacity.',
      applicabilityText:
        'Every person involved in designing or constructing or testing of pressure vessels',
      criticality: 'HIGH',
